{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-gen-12-1","title":"Genesis 12:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God calls Abram, and blesses him with a promise of Christ. 4 He departs with Lot from Haran, and comes to Canaan. 6 He journeys through Canaan, 7 which is promised to him in a vision. 10 He is driven by famine into Egypt. 11 Fear makes him feign his wife to be his sister. 14 Pharaoh, having taken her from him, by plagues is compelled to restore her. 18 He reproves Abram, whom he dismisses.</p>\n<p>had. 11:31,32; 15:7; Ne 9:7; Isa 41:9; 51:2; Eze 33:24 Get. Jos 24:2,3; Ps 45:10,11; Lu 14:26-33; Ac 7:2-6; 2Co 6:17; Heb 11:8 Re 18:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-2","title":"Genesis 12:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>13:16; 15:5; 17:5,6; 18:18; 22:17,18; 24:35; 26:4; 27:29; 28:3,14 35:11; 46:3; Ex 1:7; 32:10; Nu 14:12; 24:9,10; De 26:5; 2Sa 7:9 1Ki 3:8,9; Mic 7:20; Ro 4:11; Ga 3:7 thou shalt. 14:14-16; 18:18; 19:29; 28:4; 1Ki 1:47; Ga 3:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-3","title":"Genesis 12:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>And I. 27:29; Ex 23:22; Nu 24:9; Mt 25:40,45 in thee. 18:18; 22:18; 26:4; 28:14; 30:27,30; 39:5; Ps 72:17; Ac 3:25,26 Ro 4:11; 1Co 1:30; Ga 3:8,16,28; Eph 1:3; Col 3:11; Re 7:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-4","title":"Genesis 12:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>and Lot. 11:27 departed out. Heb 11:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-5","title":"Genesis 12:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>the souls. 14:14,21; *marg: 46:5-26 in. 11:31 and into. 10:19; Ac 7:4; Heb 11:8,9 Canaan.So called from Canaan the son of Ham, lies between the Mediterranean sea on the west, the wilderness of Paran, Idumea, and Egypt on the south, the mountains of Arabia on the east, and the mountains of Lebanon and Phoenicia on the north. Its length, from Dan to Beersheba, is about 200 miles, and its breadth, from the Mediterranean sea to its eastern borders, about 90.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-6","title":"Genesis 12:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>passed. Heb 11:9 Sichem. 33:18; 34:2; 35:4; Jos 20:7; 24:32; Jud 9:1; 1Ki 12:1 Shechem. Joh 4:5 Sychar. Ac 7:16 Sychem. plain.The word rendered \"plain\" should be rendered \"oak,\" or according to Celsius, the \"turpentine-tree.\"</p>\n<p>Moreh. De 11:30; Jud 7:1 Canaanite. 10:15,18,19; 13:7; 15:18-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-7","title":"Genesis 12:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>appeared. 17:1; 18:1; 32:30 Unto thy. 13:15; 17:3,8; 26:3; 28:13; Ex 33:1; Nu 32:11; De 1:8; 6:10; 30:20 Ps 105:9-12; Ro 9:8; Ga 3:16; 4:28 builded. 8; 8:20; 13:4,18; 26:25; 33:20; Heb 11:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-8","title":"Genesis 12:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>of Beth-el. 28:19; 35:3,15,16; Jos 8:17; 18:22; Ne 11:31 Hai. Jos 7:2; 8:3 Ai. Ne 11:31 Aija. Isa 10:28 Aiath. called. 4:26; 13:4; 21:33; Ps 116:4; Joe 2:32; Ac 2:21; Ro 10:12-14; 1Co 1:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-9","title":"Genesis 12:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>going on still. Heb. in going and journeying. 13:3; 24:62; Ps 105:13; Heb 11:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-10","title":"Genesis 12:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>A.M. 2084. B.C. 1920. was a. 26:1; 42:5; 43:1; 47:13; Ru 1:1; 2Sa 21:1; 1Ki 17:1-18:46; 2Ki 4:38 2Ki 6:25; 7:1-8:1; Ps 34:19; 107:34; Jer 14:1; Joh 16:33; Ac 7:11 Ac 14:22 went. 26:2,3; 43:1; 46:3,4; 2Ki 8:1,2; Ps 105:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-11","title":"Genesis 12:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>a fair. 14; 26:7; 29:17; 39:6,7; 2Sa 11:2; Pr 21:30; So 1:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-12","title":"Genesis 12:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>will kill. 20:11; 26:7; 1Sa 27:1; Pr 29:25; Mt 10:28; 1Jo 1:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-13","title":"Genesis 12:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Say. Joh 8:44; Ro 3:6-8; 6:23; Col 3:6 thou. 11:29; 20:2,5,12,13; 26:7; Isa 57:11; Mt 26:69-75; Ga 2:12,13 and. Ps 146:3-5; Jer 17:5-8; Eze 18:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-14","title":"Genesis 12:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>beheld. 3:6; 6:2; 39:7; Mt 5:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-15","title":"Genesis 12:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>princes. Es 2:2-16; Pr 29:12; Ho 7:4,5 Pharaoh was a common name of the Egyptian kings, and signified a \"ruler,\" or \"king,\" or \"father of his country.\"</p>\n<p>40:2; 41:1; Ex 2:5,15; 1Ki 3:1; 2Ki 18:21; Jer 25:19; 46:17; Eze 32:2 taken. 20:2; Es 2:9; Ps 105:4; Pr 6:29; Heb 13:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-16","title":"Genesis 12:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>And he. 13:2; 20:14 he had. 24:35; 26:14; 32:5,13-15; Job 1:3; 42:12; Ps 144:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-17","title":"Genesis 12:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>20:18; 1Ch 16:21; 21:22; Job 34:19; Ps 105:14,15; Heb 13:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-18","title":"Genesis 12:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>3:13; 4:10; 20:9,10; 26:9-11; 31:26; 44:15; Ex 32:21; Jos 7:19 1Sa 14:43; Pr 21:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-12-20","title":"Genesis 12:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Ex 18:27; 1Sa 29:6-11; Ps 105:14,15; Pr 21:1</p>"}]}